{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","title":"Area between two curves"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The area between two curves comes from vertical strips. Let’s compare y equals two x with y equals x squared.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Area between two curves"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.2,2.3],"y":[-0.3,4.8],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"line","y":"2*x","domain":[0,2.15],"label":"y = 2x"},{"kind":"fn","id":"parabola","y":"x^2","domain":[0,2.15],"label":"y = x²"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","step":{"id":"s2","script":"First find where the curves meet. Their intersection x values, zero and two, become our integration limits.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"intersections","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x^2=2x\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x(x-2)=0"},{"op":"equation","id":"limits","anchor":{"el":"intersections","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"a=0,\\qquad b=2"},{"op":"figure","id":"crossings","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":{"on":"line","x":0},"label":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"point","id":"finish","at":{"on":"line","x":2},"label":"(2, 4)"},{"kind":"shade","between":["line","parabola"],"from":0,"to":2}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Throughout this interval, the line is above the parabola. Each vertical strip has height upper minus lower, so integrate two x minus x squared.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"strip","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"on":"parabola","x":1.2},"to":{"on":"line","x":1.2},"label":"2x − x²"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"integral","anchor":{"el":"limits","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\int_0^2(2x-x^2)\\,dx"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Evaluate the antiderivative at two and zero. The shaded region has area four thirds square units.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"evaluation","anchor":{"el":"integral","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\left[x^2-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^2=4-\\frac83=\\frac43"},{"op":"figure","id":"answer","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0.75,0.85],"text":"A = 4/3","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.done","request_id":"dc7348f9-2133-4580-9aff-8ed275fdcbd8","accepted_steps":4,"repairs":2,"dropped_steps":0,"sanitized_steps":0,"sanitized_fields":0}
